{"name":"Lemongrass","hex":"#999a86","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemongrass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of various species of grass of the genus Cymbopogon, especially Cymbopogon citratus, which have a lemon-like taste and aroma, and are used in cooking, for tea, and for fragrance.","Sourgrass (Oxalis pes-caprae)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemongrass"}],"entries":[{"title":"LemonGrass","blocks":[{"text":"LemonGrass is a Mexican musical group, formed on August 12, 2015. The concept pays tribute to its predecessor, known as OV7, also known as La Onda Vaselina. The current members of the group are Ivanna, Sophie, Yael, Oscar, Keira, and Matias. For personal reasons, the members Jelissa, Emiliano, Paula, and Nathan had to leave the group. They have recorded 2 albums, which are LemonGrass and LemonGrass Deluxe Edition, which feature several urban songs."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LemonGrass","wikidata":"Q48965332"},{"title":"Lemongrass (music)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemongrass is a music project created by German DJ and producer Roland Voss in 1996. Voss and his brother Daniel formed the Lemongrassmusic label in 2005. Lemongrass is known for a style that mixes electronic music, EDM, downtempo, drum-n-bass, lounge, jazz, soul, trip-hop, Chillout, world music, meditation music, deep ambient, New Age, and other influences."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemongrass_(music)","wikidata":"Q1817099"},{"title":"Cymbopogon","blocks":[{"text":"Cymbopogon, also known as lemongrass, barbed wire grass, silky heads, oily heads, Cochin grass, Malabar grass, citronella grass or fever grass, is a genus of Asian, African, Australian, and tropical island plants in the grass family.\nSome species are commonly cultivated as culinary and medicinal herbs because of their scent, resembling that of lemons .\nThe name Cymbopogon derives from the Greek words kymbe and pogon \"which mean [that] in most species, the hairy spikelets project from boat-shaped spathes.\" Lemongrass and its oil are believed to possess therapeutic properties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/YosriNov04Pokok_Serai.JPG/330px-YosriNov04Pokok_Serai.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cymbopogon","wikidata":"Q5727732"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Cymbopogon_citratus_leaves.jpg/500px-Cymbopogon_citratus_leaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Cymbopogon_citratus_leaves.jpg/1280px-Cymbopogon_citratus_leaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Cymbopogon_citratus_leaves.jpg/500px-Cymbopogon_citratus_leaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"C. citratus from the Philippines, where it is locally known as tanglad","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACymbopogon_citratus_leaves.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Serai.jpg/120px-Serai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Serai.jpg/250px-Serai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Serai.jpg/120px-Serai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASerai.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Prepared_lemon_grass.JPG/120px-Prepared_lemon_grass.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Prepared_